### Smart home backend – vendor → home → supported device (catalogue) → home device
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Register a vendor (code: SAMSUNG | AMAZON | CISCO)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/vendors/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "AMAZON", "name": "Amazon"}

> {% client.global.set("vendorId", response.body.id); %}

### 2. Admin: add a supported device model with its metric mappings
#   deviceType: TV | REFRIGERATOR | AC | OVEN | WASHER | DRYER
#   metric:     TEMPERATURE (C) | POWER (W) | ENERGY (kWh) | HUMIDITY (%) | RUNTIME (min) | DOOR_OPEN_COUNT | SWITCH (1 on / 0 off)
#   conversion: NONE (default) | F_TO_C, K_TO_C (TEMPERATURE) | KW_TO_W (POWER) | WH_TO_KWH (ENERGY)
#               | SECONDS_TO_MINUTES, HOURS_TO_MINUTES (RUNTIME) – any other combination is 400
POST {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/devices/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vendorId": "{{vendorId}}",
  "deviceType": "AC",
  "model": "AZ-AC-1",
  "name": "Amazon Smart AC",
  "mappings": [
    { "externalMetric": "powerConsumption", "metric": "POWER", "conversion": "KW_TO_W" },
    { "externalMetric": "energyUsage", "metric": "ENERGY" },
    { "externalMetric": "temperature", "metric": "TEMPERATURE", "conversion": "NONE" },
    { "externalMetric": "powerState", "metric": "SWITCH" }
  ]
}

> {% client.global.set("deviceId", response.body.id); %}

### 2b. Admin: replace all mappings of that device (full set, not a patch)
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/devices/{{deviceId}}/mappings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mappings": [
    { "externalMetric": "powerConsumption", "metric": "POWER", "conversion": "KW_TO_W" },
    { "externalMetric": "energyUsage", "metric": "ENERGY" },
    { "externalMetric": "powerState", "metric": "SWITCH" }
  ]
}

### 2c. Invalid: conversion does not fit the metric → 400
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/devices/{{deviceId}}/mappings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mappings": [ { "externalMetric": "temperature", "metric": "TEMPERATURE", "conversion": "KW_TO_W" } ] }

### 3. User: browse supported devices (filters optional)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/devices?vendorId={{vendorId}}&deviceType=AC

### 4. Register a home (timezone optional, default UTC)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/homes/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "My home", "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata"}

> {% client.global.set("homeId", response.body.id); %}

### 5. User: register their appliance in the home (pollingIntervalSeconds optional, default 300)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/home-devices/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "homeId": "{{homeId}}",
  "deviceId": "{{deviceId}}",
  "externalDeviceId": "amz-ac-01",
  "name": "Bedroom AC",
  "pollingIntervalSeconds": 60
}

> {% client.global.set("homeDeviceId", response.body.id); %}

### Get vendor / home / device / home device
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/vendors/{{vendorId}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/homes/{{homeId}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/devices/{{deviceId}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/home-devices/{{homeDeviceId}}

### Lists: what's already there
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/vendors

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/homes

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/smart-home/home-devices?homeId={{homeId}}
